  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0) or shows recent negative momentum.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoot after sharp price spikes by applying a 10-15% dampening factor to the immediate next period.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent low prices when sentiment is positive (sentiment > 0) to capture mean reversion.",
    "Apply a lag correction: if true outcome is significantly lower than forecast, adjust next forecast by +0.5 to 1.0 units to avoid underestimating rebound.",
    "When sentiment is neutral or positive and price is trending upward, increase forecast by 1-2% to account for momentum bias.",
    "For periods with high volatility (e.g., > 5% daily change), reduce forecast confidence and apply a smoothing filter to avoid overreaction."
  ]
}
